message.content:
Design task: the user wants the dashboard footer's "About these numbers" section (C-25, with footnote lines C-09…C-14) to be "more presentable, organized and easier to digest". Their screenshot of the current build is /Users/josemejia/Desktop/Screenshot 2026-09-29 at 9.44.46 AM.png (Read it). Today it's a heading on the left and six loose lines in a two-column flow, with no grouping: the method notes, the data facts and "Data as of" are all mixed.

Read CLAUDE.md, docs/acceptance-criteria.md (C-09…C-14, C-25, C-26, UI-06, UI-13, UI-19, UI-20b, UI-22, UI-47: which lines appear when; for example, C-14 only shows for a single activity type, and "Data as of" only once there is data), docs/design/Spec.dc.html (the approved tokens and type) and docs/design/Main.dc.html (the current footer), plus the implemented footer in web/src/app/features/dashboard/dashboard.page.ts.

Produce 2–3 genuinely different footer options, for example:
- grouped columns with small subheads (e.g. "How it's compared" / "What's counted" / "Freshness");
- a compact fact strip with icons for the key facts (8-week baseline, de-duplicated, inbound events) and the caveats below it;
- "Data as of" promoted to a clear freshness badge, separate from the method notes.
Each option must:
- keep every footnote line's text VERBATIM (it's approved copy that tests check); any new subheads or labels are copy proposals for product;
- show both states: the "All activity" view, without C-14, and a single-type view, with C-14 (e.g. account 6, Leads, week of Jun 29);
- follow the approved visual system (Geist, tokens, desktop only);
- stay accessible: real headings or lists, icons aria-hidden, contrast ≥ 4.5:1.

Output: new artboards `FooterOptionA.dc.html`, `FooterOptionB.dc.html` and optionally `FooterOptionC.dc.html`, each showing the footer area at 1440 wide (you can crop to the bottom of the page), in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-josemejia-Documents-Software-Development-Qualitara-relay-activity-health/74b25094-c0f6-4b4a-a9ba-66244c7b622d/scratchpad/canvas/project/. Add them to canvas.json as a new titled row, "Footer options", below the "Picker follow-up" row, keeping every other key and entry exactly as it is. Format rules: .../scratchpad/canvas-ref/CANVAS-FORMAT-BRIEF.md. Don't touch the other artboards; don't render, publish or commit.

Handoff report in the CLAUDE.md format. Under ## Uncertain, give each option's motivation and main trade-off, your recommendation, the copy proposals, and any test or acceptance impact (e.g. UI-06 structure).

